 ('rules','Validation & rules','Describe acceptable inputs and visible exceptions','Validation records input rules. Conditional formatting displays conditions. Neither is a substitute for verifying programmatic writes.','Lists, bounds, custom rules, scales, bars and icons.','Range → validation / conditional formats',[['Type','rule token','List, numeric bound, custom formula, color scale and others.'],['Formula / threshold','value or expression','The condition that the rule evaluates.'],['Presentation','format object','What the reader sees when the condition holds.']]),
 ('tables','Excel Tables','Turn a rectangle into a named dataset','An Excel Table adds headers, a name and structured references to a rectangular dataset. It is different from a pivot or a sensitivity grid.','Create, append, style, set headers/totals and remove.','Worksheet → table → data rows',[['range','A1 address','Full table footprint.'],['hasHeaders','boolean','Whether the first row contains field names.'],['showTotals','boolean','Reserve a row: this version does not insert one.'],['rows.add index','null','Appending works; indexed insertion is unsupported.']]),
 ('sensitivity','What-If tables','Ask how one result changes across inputs','A What-If Data Table repeatedly substitutes scenario inputs into an existing calculation and records the results.','One- and two-variable sensitivity grids.','Formula + scenario headers → projected body',[['fullRange','A1 address','Include the corner formula, headers and output body.'],['rowInput','single cell','Replaced by scenario values across the top.'],['columnInput','single cell','Replaced by scenario values down the left.'],['recalculate','method call','Required after constructing the table.']]),
 ('pivots','Pivots & slicers','Summarize records by category','A pivot aggregates source rows. A slicer filters its categories. Cached summaries and the written output area both need checks.','Group fields, aggregate, filter and rebuild caches.','Source → cache → pivot → slicer',[['Source / destination','ranges','Which records are summarized, and where the result appears.'],['Hierarchies','field names','Rows, columns and data measures.'],['Creation route','workbook.pivotTables','The tested root route allows a slicer to find its pivot.']]),
 ('charts','Charts','Give the numbers a visual form','Charts bind a visual object to data. The in-memory object, rendered picture and native Excel chart are separate outputs.','Create, bind, style, annotate, position and remove.','Worksheet ranges → series → chart',[['Type','25 enum tokens','Only 16 emitted native chart XML in the tested fixtures.'],['Data','ranges or arrays','Range references retain the link to workbook cells.'],['Anchor','cells / pixels','Position and size on the worksheet.'],['Labels / data table','existing facade','Mutate nested fields; plain-object replacement can break export.']]),
 ('drawings','Images, shapes & sparklines','Add visual objects and small trends','Images carry pixels, shapes carry geometry and text, and sparklines display a series inside a cell. Each has its own placement and lifecycle.','Add, replace, arrange, style and delete.','Worksheet → drawing or sparkline group',[['Source','bytes / SVG / path','Image insertion does not extract editable cells.'],['Geometry','190 tokens','Custom geometry also needs path commands.'],['Sparkline type','line / column / stacked','Three distinct small-series views.'],['Anchor','from + to / extent','Set at creation or use the supported update operation.']]),
 ('names','Names','Give reusable references a meaning','A defined name gives a range or function a stable name. Scope decides whether it belongs to the workbook or a single sheet.','Named ranges and named LAMBDA functions.','Workbook or worksheet → defined name',[['Name / scope','string / owner','Avoid ambiguous worksheet and workbook definitions.'],['Range','qualified address','The cells a name refers to.'],['lambda','expression','The working property for named functions; not formula.']]),
